  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SUPPORTING CIVIL SOCIETY TO REDUCE ILLEGAL CONSUMPTION AND TRADE OF ENDANGERED TORTOISE AND FRESHWATER TURTLES IN CHINA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO IMPLEMENT CONSERVATION PROGRAMS TO REDUCE THE DEMAND FOR TORTOISES AND FRESHWATER TURTLES (TFT) FOR FOOD, MEDICINE AND PETS IN CHINA, THE WORLD S LARGEST CONSUMER OF TRAFFICKED TFT. ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) REVIEWING CHINA S REGULATIONS ON TFT FARMING AND TRADE (2) BUILDING THE CAPACITY OF CIVIL SOCIETY TO SUPPORT TFT CONSERVATION AND MONITORING (3) PROVIDING INFORMATION TO IMPROVE TRAINING MATERIALS FOR CUSTOMS AGENTS AND OTHER RELEVANT PERSONNEL IN PRIORITY AREAS OF GUANGDONG, GUANGXI AND FUJIAN IN ORDER TO BOLSTER THEIR SURVEILLANCE CAPACITY AND (4) WORKING WITH BEHAVIORAL INSIGHTS TEAM (A LEADING ORGANIZATION THAT GENERATES BEHAVIORAL INSIGHTS FOR SOCIAL CHANGE) TO DESIGN AND CONDUCT A DEMAND REDUCTION CAMPAIGN TARGETING SPECIFIC POPULATIONS IN LOCATIONS OF HIGH TFT TRADE, E.G. GUANGDONG PROVINCE.</narrative>
  </description>
